{"command":"cat > /fs04/ar57/wenyu/GeneRec/results/research/issue117/runs/run_4053f2250f914d4e/agents/geometry/candidate.json <<'EOF'
{"schema_version":1,"candidate_id":"geometry-poincare-residual-sid-v2","behavior_problem_id":"directional-next-item-transition-with-high-nonreverse-rate","behavior_evidence_sha256":"793d52dce39a5a8aa3963ff566ae50612114b9d20d31227dfed3d1e9fc653b9b","literature_evidence_sha256":"8ba6837c216074f407682b678f8b30acb30e89d57086da57dd7a4d6a599d9d0d","next_item_hypothesis":"Demonstrated failure: content-only item codes may merge distinct successors of an anchor into indistinguishable first-level neighborhoods despite train-only directed transitions: 314605 of 339519 transitions have no observed reverse event (0.9266197178950221), and mean next-item entropy is 4.844072338042215 bits. Hypothesis: negative curvature better represents branching, non-reversible successor neighborhoods than a flat metric, improving hierarchical item codes and ultimately Stage3 next-item ranking. These observations do not establish causality or curvature necessity. Stage2 builds one global three-token SID per item from content and does not rank or use user context.","math_definition":{"builder":"For each item i, fixed content embedding e_i maps through the same frozen encoder f_theta to z_i in R^32. Set r_i^(1)=z_i. At each level j=1,2,3 perform in exact order: MAP residual r_i^(j) -> PROJECT u_i^(j)=P_R(r_i^(j)) -> ASSIGN k_ij=argmin over k in 1..256 of D_c^2(u_i^(j),P_R(q_jk)) -> SUBTRACT r_i^(j+1)=r_i^(j)-q_j,k_ij. The subtraction result is not projected until the next level's MAP then projection. Code vectors are constrained by projection after every optimizer update. Level 2 conditions exactly on k_i1 through its residual; level 3 conditions exactly on k_i1 and k_i2 through its residual. SID=(k_i1,k_i2,k_i3), globally shared for each item.","geometry":{"shared_map":"P_R(x)=x*min(1,R/||x||), P_R(0)=0, R=0.99. It is identical and curvature-independent in both arms. Every vector entering a distance, including residual maps and code vectors, is projected to ||x||<=R.","curvature":0.1,"epsilon":1e-7,"clamp_domain_policy":"For nonidentical x,y compute t=2*c*||x-y||^2/((1-c*||x||^2)*(1-c*||y||^2)); evaluate arcosh(1+max(t,epsilon)). For exactly identical vectors return zero, bypassing clamp. R ensures positive denominators for c=0.1. The flat branch uses its exact analytic limit and the same exact-coincidence convention.","scored_distance":"D^2(x,y)=d_c(x,y)^2=(1/c)*arcosh(1+2*c*||x-y||^2/((1-c*||x||^2)*(1-c*||y||^2)))^2. Assignments and objective use squared distance in both arms. Stable arcosh(1+t)=log1p(t+sqrt(t*(t+2))) for t>=0 after clamp, with exact coincidence handled separately. As c->0, D^2 tends exactly to 4*||x-y||^2; unsquared distance tends to 2*||x-y||.","c_dependent_rules_and_limits":"The scored-distance rule has c->0 limit 4*||x-y||^2. No exponential map is used; if present as an identity operation its value and limit are identity. Projection radius (1-epsilon)/sqrt(c) is not used; it is undefined at c=0, where the flat arm instead uses the shared fixed P_R with R=0.99. Projection and residual rules have no c dependence.","flat_arm":"One implementation parameterized by c=0.1 or c=0. The flat branch evaluates the exact squared-distance limit 4*||x-y||^2. Encoder, projection, assignments, code parameters, residual subtraction, losses, initialization, optimizer, schedule, seeds, and budget are identical. Only distance expression changes."},"objective":{"anti_collapse":"L_rec is the anti-collapse mechanism, with weight 1: each item's content-derived z_i must reconstruct from detached selected code vectors. Mapping every item to the same SID incurs content-dependent residual error and cannot erase this term.","loss_equations":["For train item set I, B=|I|, z_i=f_theta(e_i), a_ij=stopgrad(q_j,k_ij), and xhat_i=sum(j=1..3) a_ij. L_rec=(1/B)*sum(i in I) D_c^2(P_R(z_i),P_R(xhat_i)). Arithmetic mean over I; empty I invalidates run.","L_commit=(1/(3B))*sum(i in I)sum(j=1..3) D_c^2(P_R(r_i^(j)),stopgrad(P_R(q_j,k_ij))). Arithmetic mean over item-level pairs; selected code target detached; empty I invalidates run.","Let T be multiset of adjacent item transitions from train split only. For each (a,b) in T choose n(a,b) as lowest-ID item in I excluding a,b; omit examples if no such item. T' is retained examples. With s_i=concat(onehot(k_i1),onehot(k_i2),onehot(k_i3)), L_trans=(1/|T'|)*sum((a,b) in T') max(0,1-cos(s_a,s_b)+cos(s_a,s_n(a,b))). Cosine norm denominator adds 1e-12. If T' empty, L_trans=0.","L=L_rec+0.25*L_commit+0.1*L_trans. Each term is normalized as stated; train transitions are legal assignment supervision, not Stage2 ranking."],"assignment_target_circularity":"Current-parameter hard argmin indices are treated as nondifferentiable. Reconstruction selected-code vectors and commitment target code vectors are stop-gradient, so target gradients do not flow through their assignments or target vectors."},"diagnostics":{"definitions":"Use the frozen definitions verbatim: valid L1 positive hit rate over 52855 frozen validation pairs (one positive plus ten negatives per anchor, seed 42, history[-1] -> target), share whose anchor item's first SID token equals positive's first token; valid Hard-L1 ER=10*positive_hits/negative_hits with negatives counted identically; level2_distinct_prefixes=|{(k1,k2)}| over all items; L3 collision=share of items whose complete triple is shared by another; L3 refinement gain=mean item log2(|bucket(k1,k2)|/|bucket(k1,k2,k3)|); conditional G3 uses alpha=1,K=256, p_pref(l)=(number of items sharing target's level-two prefix with third code l, minus one only for target's own third code, plus alpha)/(bucket size minus one plus alpha*K); p_hist(l)=(train-only longest-prefix successor count of anchor restricted to successors sharing target's level-two prefix and third code l, plus alpha*p_pref(l))/(restricted successor total plus alpha); average log2(p_hist(target third code)/p_pref(target third code)); pair with no restricted successor contributes 0, non-finite pair NULL. No definition is changed.","validation_role":"Diagnostics only. Validation pairs and behavior never enter fitting, target construction, assignments, or SID creation."}},"hyperbolic_necessity":"Negative curvature is motivated by a branching neighborhood: negatively curved space can expand neighborhood capacity with radius, potentially separating successor branches under a fixed-depth hierarchy. Strong train-only directionality and successor entropy motivate testing this; neither measurements nor literature establish necessity. The cited generative semantic-ID work supports semantic-ID recommendation only; supplied hyperbolic overlap is unverified.","euclidean_control":"Identical c-parameterized implementation, at c=0.1 versus c=0. Same P_R, model, code parameters, assignments, residual updates, train-only transition signal, objective, initialization, optimizer, schedule, seeds, and budget. Only scored squared distance changes to its exact c->0 limit; no curvature-dependent representation map exists.","effect_site":"Stage2 assignment and reconstruction/commitment geometry, with leading indicators L3 collision, L3 refinement gain, conditional G3, and prefix diversity; Stage3 T5 ranking is the behavioral endpoint.","real_trigger_measurement":"Train-only longest-prefix evidence: directed_pairs=323633, transitions=339519, no_observed_reverse_events=314605, no_reverse_fraction=0.9266197178950221, mean_next_item_entropy_bits=4.844072338042215. Descriptive, not causal.","training_only_inputs":"Stage2 uses item content embeddings and adjacent train-split transitions only. No validation/test behavior, future event, prediction-time user context, or batch composition enters fitting, targets, assignments, or global SID creation. Validation is diagnostic-only; test interactions are Stage3 evaluation-only.","stable_global_sid":true,"protocol":{"latent_dim":32,"levels":3,"codes_per_level":256,"hyperparameter_sweep":false,"uses_future_events":false,"epochs":3000,"batch_size":"frozen existing Stage2 batch size, unchanged between arms","optimizer_schedule":"frozen existing Stage2 optimizer and schedule, unchanged between arms","seeds":"frozen existing Stage2 seed set, paired identically","codebook_initialization":"frozen existing Stage2 codebook initialization, identical paired initialization","compute_budget":"identical frozen Stage2 budget","forbidden_components":["prefix Transformer","beam search","NDCG/Recall in Stage2","user bootstrap","new training protocol"]},"falsifier":{"stage2_diagnostics":[{"name":"valid_l1_hard_er","direction":"curved > flat and curved strictly above frozen Resample reference","minimum_effect":"curved value strictly greater than 16.38953942232631","seed_rule":"For each paired frozen seed compute curved-minus-flat and require every difference >0; arithmetic mean of curved seed values must exceed 16.38953942232631. Equal seed weighting."},{"name":"level2_distinct_prefixes","direction":"curved > flat and curved strictly above frozen threshold","minimum_effect":"curved value strictly greater than 16145","seed_rule":"For each paired frozen seed compute curved-minus-flat and require every difference >0; arithmetic mean of curved seed values must exceed 16145. Equal seed weighting."},{"name":"L3 collision","direction":"curved < flat","minimum_effect":"mean paired absolute reduction >=0.01","seed_rule":"Compute flat-minus-curved per paired seed; every difference >0 and unweighted arithmetic mean >=0.01."},{"name":"L3 refinement gain","direction":"curved > flat","minimum_effect":"mean paired increase >=0.10 bits","seed_rule":"Compute curved-minus-flat per paired seed; every difference >0 and unweighted arithmetic mean >=0.10 bits."},{"name":"conditional G3","direction":"curved > flat","minimum_effect":"mean paired increase >=0.05 bits","seed_rule":"Compute curved-minus-flat per paired seed using frozen estimator; every difference >0 and unweighted arithmetic mean >=0.05 bits."}],"stage3_behavioral_test":{"metric":"test_R@10","direction":"curved > flat","minimum_effect":"mean paired absolute increase >=0.005","seed_rule":"On identical paired seeds compute curved test_R@10 minus flat test_R@10 per seed; take unweighted arithmetic mean and require >=0.005. No metric substitution."},"classification":{"falsified_if":"Any registered diagnostic or Stage3 test has a defined aggregate in the opposite direction or fails its registered minimum_effect; use only registered thresholds and rules.","passed_if":"All five registered Stage2 diagnostics and Stage3 test satisfy their registered direction and minimum_effect with no NULL seed; use only registered thresholds and rules.","mixed_if":"At least one Stage2 diagnostic satisfies direction and minimum_effect and at least one registered Stage2 diagnostic or Stage3 test fails direction or minimum_effect, with no NULL seed; use only registered thresholds and rules."},"null_outcome_rule":"If any seed-wise or aggregate change is undefined or non-finite (zero denominator, missing evaluation, empty stratum), classify NULL. Any comparison with any NULL seed is inconclusive, neither passed nor falsified; never impute or drop that seed."}}
